  "description": "Answers frozen from libsodium 1.0.22's release build (the crate libsodium-sys-stable 1.24.0 bundles the 1.0.22-RELEASE source tree): the XChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD, crypto_box_easy and the secretstream, at lengths from 0 to 1,048,577 bytes. Each case holds the SHA-256 of the whole sealed output and its 16-byte authenticator. They are never made again to make a failure go away: an implementation that does not reproduce them is the one that is wrong.",
  "name": "cipher-known-answers",
  "rule": [
    "Every plaintext, key, nonce, seed, header and additional datum is the first N bytes of a stream whose block n is SHA-256(label, 0x00, n as eight big-endian bytes), blocks in order.",
    "aead: key kr-known-answers/aead/key; plaintext kr-known-answers/aead/plaintext/<length>; additional data of aad_bytes bytes kr-known-answers/aead/aad/<aad_bytes>; 24-byte nonce kr-known-answers/aead/nonce/<length>/<aad_bytes>; sealed is the ciphertext and then the 16-byte tag.",
    "box: seeds kr-known-answers/box/seed/sender and kr-known-answers/box/seed/recipient give the two keypairs through crypto_box_seed_keypair; plaintext kr-known-answers/box/plaintext/<length>; 24-byte nonce kr-known-answers/box/nonce/<length>; sealed by the sender's secret key for the recipient's public key, authenticator first.",
    "stream: key kr-known-answers/stream/key and 24-byte header kr-known-answers/stream/header, which a push starts from through a pulling state that init_pull makes from them; record i holds plaintext kr-known-answers/stream/plaintext/<i> of the i-th length, pushed under tag 0, 1, 0, 2 in turn and tag 3 on the last record."
  ],
